          "settings": {
            "title": "Configuration data",
            "body": "<p><strong>Cell chemistry:</strong> LFP<br><strong>Rated voltage:</strong> 51.2V<br><strong>Rated capacity:</strong> 200Ah / 10.24kWh<br><strong>Max charging voltage:</strong> 57.6V<br><strong>Overdischarge voltage:</strong> 44.8V<br><strong>Max / peak charging current:</strong> 150A / 190A<br><strong>Max / peak discharging current:</strong> 200A / 220A<br><strong>Cycle life:</strong> 5,000 cycles<br><strong>Weight:</strong> 88kg<br><strong>Dimensions (H × W × D):</strong> 1165 × 525 × 170mm<br><strong>Enclosure rating:</strong> IP54<br><strong>Installation:</strong> wall mounting or floor standing</p>\n<p>Communication interfaces include CAN, RS485, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth for monitoring through the battery or inverter interface.</p>",
            "asset_name": "",
            "image_alt": "",
            "image_caption": ""
          }
        },
        "manual_2": {
          "type": "manual_section",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Before installation",
            "body": "<ol><li>Review the inverter communication and electrical specifications before installation.</li><li>Confirm the delivery destination and any local receiving requirements.</li><li>Use a qualified installer and follow local electrical requirements.</li><li>Confirm that the mounting surface, clearance and cable routing suit the selected wall or floor position; WL10B is heavier than WL5A and needs suitable fixing.</li></ol>",
            "asset_name": "",
            "image_alt": "",
            "image_caption": ""
          }
        },
        "manual_3": {
          "type": "manual_section",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Monitoring and communication",
            "body": "<p>WL10B communicates over CAN and RS485 with the inverter or system controller, and additionally lists Wi-Fi and Bluetooth for monitoring. Up to nine sets can be connected in one system; confirm the exact configuration with your installer before purchase.</p>",
            "asset_name": "",
            "image_alt": "",
            "image_caption": ""
          }
        },
        "manual_4": {
          "type": "manual_section",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Safety and handling",
            "body": "<ol><li>Installation and wiring must be carried out by a qualified installer.</li><li>Verify polarity and torque all connections before commissioning.</li><li>Keep the battery away from water, heat sources, sparks and open flames.</li><li>Do not open, modify or repair the battery enclosure.</li><li>Do not connect loads or chargers outside the ratings listed above.</li><li>Follow local electrical code for breakers, fuses and disconnects.</li></ol>",
            "asset_name": "",
            "image_alt": "",
            "image_caption": ""
          }
        },
        "manual_5": {
          "type": "manual_section",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Documents and certification status",
            "body": "<p>No model-matched installation manual, certification, UN38.3 report or safety data sheet is published on this page. Before ordering, contact product support with the battery configuration, inverter model and firmware, installation location and US delivery ZIP code. Ask support to confirm compatibility and which applicable documents can be supplied for that exact configuration. Do not install or commission the system until the required instructions and documents have been reviewed with your installer.</p>",
            "asset_name": "",
            "image_alt": "",
            "image_caption": ""
